# Terraform
.terraform/
crash.log
*.tfplan

# Provider lock files ARE committed. A module pinned by tag with providers left
# to float is half a pin, and the floating half is the dangerous one: the
# bpg/proxmox constraint here is ~> 0.101, which admits everything below 1.0 on
# a provider whose own comments call the SDN resources "still settling". A fresh
# init could therefore resolve a provider that plans a replacement against live
# SDN objects.
#
# State holds resource detail; keep it in VCS per architecture/tenant/building.md
# ("VCS for small deployments"), but never the backups or any *.tfvars that
# might carry a token.
*.tfstate.backup
*.auto.tfvars
secrets.auto.tfvars

# Rendered credentials, if anyone copies one in here
*.env

# Terraform lock files from an interrupted run
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
